# Adding a table

Each table is one row in **Tables** (`Config.Tables`). The script places the table, the board and both chairs itself, so nothing needs to be built in the map.

## Steps

1. Stand where the middle of the table should be, facing the way the white chair should face.
2. Open `/poggy`, pick **Chess & Checkers**, then **Tables**.
3. Press **Add table**.
4. Give it an **Id**. It is saved with every game played there, so keep it once games have been played. Use letters, numbers and underscores.
5. Give it a **Name**. Players see it above the prompts and on the table screens.
6. On **Position**, press **use my position**. On **Heading**, use your heading.
7. Save, then restart the script.

## Tips

- The whole table turns with **Heading**. At 0 the white chair is on the east side.
- Two tables can stand close together. Each has its own props and its own game, and players can watch both.
- Players see the furniture within **Show distance** (20 m by default). Each player places the props on their own screen, so keep the distance modest.
- To hide a table from the map, turn off **Show map blip**. The table still works.
- To remove a table, delete its row. Its past games stay in everyone's record.
- `/chesstable` lists every table and what is happening at it. `/chesstable reset <id>` ends a stuck game there (with no result, and any wager returned) and stands both players up.
